  "body": "Closes #823\nClaim: cloud/i823-sonnet\nAuthor model: sonnet-5.5 (cloud/i823-sonnet)\nReviewer model: opus-5.5 (cloud/r948-opus)\n\n**Problem**: the \"Page …\" entry of the reader's page menus opened a system alert with an empty field; legacy opens the \"Page numéro\" sheet.\n\n**Cause**: the alert was a placeholder (LOT-186).\n\n**Change**: `ReaderPageSheet` ports `TopicPagePickerSheet` / `TopicPagePickerQuickButton` (`HFRswift/Swift/Common.swift:3063-3190` @ 87fe0d1c): \"Choisir une page entre 1 et N\", first | field | last, -10 | -1 | +1 | +10, \"Valider\", close, 260 pt detent. Field prefilled with the current page. The rules are a pure `ReaderPagePicker` (clamp, step, resolved page, target). The alert and its `pageText` state are removed. Same entry, same two menus. Follow-up (topic list row, button tint): #949.\n\n**Tests** (`ReaderChromeTests`, fail without the change: the type does not exist): `theSheetStepsAndClampsAsLegacyDoes`, `theSheetOpensOnlyAPageOfTheTopic`. `swiftlint lint --strict` clean. Not compiled here (Linux): reviewed with compiler rigour.\n\n**Device checks** (do not block the merge):\n- Sheet opens from \"Page …\" in both menus, field shows the current page, number pad shows.\n- Detent 260 pt fits on iPhone and Duo cover screen; keyboard does not hide the buttons.\n- Valider opens the page; disabled on empty / 0 / > last.\n- Visual match with legacy (system tint, #949).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJYN61sLN42WtLoq1P",
