   "body": "Reviewer model: opus-5.5 (cloud/r948-opus)\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r948-opus, head 76c7936): APPROVE** — head 76c793628c28ea75014130d25c0910971deba088\n\n1. **Low**: `ReaderPageSheet.swift:55-57`. The port comment says the field \"opens on the current page where legacy opened on its own last input\". That is wrong: legacy also fills in the current page every time the sheet opens (`Common.swift:3532`, `MessagesView.swift:4937`, `MainWindow.swift:454` @ 87fe0d1c). The comment also starts \"Differences: none intended\" and then lists one. Fix: the only difference is the system tint instead of `themePalette.actionTintColor` / `.systemGray3`. Name GAP-060, as AGENTS §4 asks.\n2. **Low**: the PR body. The comment promises a \"GAP-060 follow-up\" for the tint, but no issue was opened for it.\n3. **Low** (outside #823's scope): `TopicListView.swift:111-122` still opens a system alert for \"Page numéro\"; legacy uses the same `TopicPagePickerSheet` from the topic row menu (`Common.swift:3586-3591, 3724-3731` @ 87fe0d1c). Fix: a follow-up issue.\n4. **Detail**: `ReaderWebView.swift:58` still names the \"Aller à la page\" prompt.\n\nChecked with no finding: stepping and limits match legacy `resolvedPage`, Valider disabled until the field holds a page in 1…last (`isInputValid`), 260 pt height, Fermer and Valider; `model.page` is never nil again so the sheet cannot come up empty; typed text survives a reload (`@State` set once); closures on the main actor. Verified by reading the diff against legacy at `87fe0d1c`, #823 and the PR body; `swiftlint lint --strict` clean at 76c7936. Nothing compiled or tested (Linux).\n\n**Author response (round 1, head e28d7b5)**: 1 and 4 fixed (comment now names the tint only, GAP-060, `Common.swift:3532`; stale prompt comment updated). 2 and 3 recorded in #949 (topic list row reuse, tint). No re-review: comment-only changes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
